  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `align_part_cylinder` and `place_setup_origin` to the MCP tool registry.\nCall the same undoable commands as the GUI.\nKeep the cylinder axis landing check and the WCS rotation.\nRefuse malformed arguments and unchanged origins by name.\nDocument both tools in the MCP skill table.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe orientation dropdown backends shipped without MCP tools.\nAgents could not call these command paths.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll three pins failed on unchanged production code and now pass:\n\n- `orientation_tools_are_listed`\n- `align_part_cylinder_lands_undoes_and_refuses_by_name`\n- `place_setup_origin_moves_named_setup_keeps_rotation_and_undoes`\n\nRestoring upstream's original MCP file made all three pins fail.\nRestoring the fix made them pass.\nSeven individual guard mutations also failed, then passed after restoration: target, angle, source, point, vertex with point, box with pick, and unchanged origin.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed with 326 passed and one ignored.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe first gate attempt stopped before testing because sccache lost its server connection.\nRestarting the cache server resolved it.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` was empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo GUI interaction or physical machine run was exercised.\nThe pins exercise target X and valid angles through MCP.\nThey do not force the backend's numerical axis-landing failure branch.\nThe implementation delegates that check to the existing command.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone of the changed files appeared in the open PR overlap checks.\nThe branch starts at upstream main `4f4edcf35465c3ee83d7d4197685fc0e661e52f1`, as requested.\nUpstream advanced with an unrelated merge during verification.\n\nEffort: high.\n\nChangelog: Expose cylinder alignment and setup origin placement as undoable MCP tools with named refusals.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #1586\n\n",
